Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not a clinical-judgment-replacement.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not an individualized-person-centered-care-replacement.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline and there is a health-care-professional then it is recommended that the health-care-professional does not apply the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline as an inflexible-standard.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline and there is a health-system then it is recommended that the health-system does not apply the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline as an inflexible-standard.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline and there is a pharmacy then it is recommended that the pharmacy does not apply the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline as an inflexible-standard.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline and there is a third-party-payer then it is recommended that the third-party-payer does not apply the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline as an inflexible-standard.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline and there is a governmental-jurisdiction then it is recommended that the governmental-jurisdiction does not apply the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline as an inflexible-standard.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline then it is recommended that the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline does not cause an opioid-taper that occurs rapidly.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline then it is recommended that the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline does not cause an opioid-discontinuation that occurs abruptly.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not a clinical-practice-law.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not a clinical-practice-regulation.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not a clinical-practice-policy.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not an FDA-approved-labeling-substitute.
If a patient has a sickle-cell-disease-pain then it is false that a recommendation applies to the patient.
If a patient has a cancer-related-pain then it is false that a recommendation applies to the patient.
If a patient receives a palliative-care then it is false that a recommendation applies to the patient.
If a patient receives an end-of-life-care then it is false that a recommendation applies to the patient.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not an opioid-use-disorder-medication-guideline.
